  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge is slowly progressing into the Quad State \nregion for the weekend as a very large area of surface high \npressure remains centered near New England. Patchy morning fog \nis possible, mainly near rivers and lakes.\n\nLow pressure tracks northeastward from the Front Range to the\nNorthern Great Lakes early next week, but its cold front and\nassociated precipitation are expected to stay well to the north\nof the Quad State as high pressure shifts towards the Mid- \nAtlantic. A resurgence of the ridge, and continued stagnation \nof the surface high, keeps rain out of the forecast through the\nworkweek. Throughout the weekend and the week ahead, highs are \nforecast in the mid 70s to near 80 and lows generally in the \nmid-40s to near 50.\n\nAt the end of the week, troughing develops in the west and the\nridge shifts just enough to potentially bring rain to end the\nmonth next weekend, more of a trick rather than a treat.",
